// Title: Deletion of Volume Shadow Copies via WMI with PowerShell
// Sigma ID: 21ff4ca9-f13a-41ad-b828-0077b2af2e40
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-20 | Modified: 2022-12-30
// ATT&CK: impact, T1490
// Description: Detects deletion of Windows Volume Shadow Copies with PowerShell code and Get-WMIObject. This
//   technique is used by numerous ransomware families such as Sodinokibi/REvil
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1490/T1490.md#atomic-test-5---windows---delete-volume-shadow-copies-via-wmi-with-powershell
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/volume-shadow-copy-deletion-via-powershell.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_shadowcopy_deletion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-WmiObject" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gwmi" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-CimInstance" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gcim") and ProcessCommandLine contains "Win32_ShadowCopy" and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".Delete()" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Remove-WmiObject" or ProcessCommandLine contains "rwmi" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Remove-CimInstance" or ProcessCommandLine contains "rcim")
